So far, I've been able to modify the generate_tests so it generates all of the tests, though there are repeats--I can't seem to find a way to generate the test cases without repeating everything including doubles (i.e. normal_log(double,double,double) is repeated four extra times). The issue here is that I can't just throw everything into the argument list when I generate the tests since we can't have something like normal_log(fvar<double>, var, double) so I generated everything with some variation of fvar<double>,var,fvar<fvar<double>>,fvar<var>,fvar<fvar<var>> separately.

The main issue I'm having right now is that when testing gradients and finite diffs, the code is different for fvar<var>,var,fvar<double>, fvar<fvar<double>>, and fvar<fvar<var>> (not to mention we want to test higher orders for the fvar<fvar< > > ones). So we could have all of this in one file which would probably be quite messy with all the enable_ifs or specializations or we can have 5 different files (one for fvar<double>, one for fvar<var>, one for fvar<fvar<double>>, one for fvar<fvar<var>>, and one for var). If we go with the latter (which I think would probably be easier to implement), that would mean that we would have some duplicate code (namely, all of the tests that don't involve gradients).

Thoughts?

