On Jun 24, 2014, at 6:29 PM, Daniel Lee <bea...@alum.mit.edu> wrote:

> Hi Allen,
>
> Thanks for the reminder! If we can get a C interface out, I think we could dance around Rcpp and Julia integration would be easy.

I think it'd be great to get rid of the Rcpp dependency,
as it seems very brittle.

What would a C interface look like from the R side
and how would we have to restrict our output?

Hadley has a page up about it:

  http://adv-r.had.co.nz/C-interface.html#c-data-structures

It looks really ugly.  I see some other wrappers, but those
look like add-on packages like Rcpp, so we'd have to make sure
we're not just jumping out of the frying pan and into the fire.

- Bob

